schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-UISETUP
wu: E-UISETUP.W6
tests:
  unit:
    count: 21
    covers: "Rust store.rs (+1): note_connection increments connection_count and broadcasts ConnectionSeen { authority }, count independent of flow inserts/evictions. Rust api/view.rs (+1 case): ConnectionSeen maps to SSE 'connection' with { authority }. TS setup.test.ts (+13): the status-derivation functions return the right cell for every (probe, decrypted, traffic, running, error) combination — trustStatus (probe-trusted green; decrypted proves trust; traffic-not-decrypting = warn device-hint; un-probeable = can't-check; probed-untrusted-nothing = calm muted; installing/failed transients; AND an authoritative positive beats a stale error), proxyStatus (probe-ours or ANY connection = green; nothing-yet vs can't-check distinct; positive beats stale error), verifyStatus (green only on a decrypted flow), proveItSnippet carries the real address. TS api.test.ts (+2): connectionCount reads /stats; stream() routes a 'connection' event to onConnection ONLY, never onEvent (no /flows refetch for a bare tunnel). TS Onboarding.test.tsx: honest status line per derivation (trusted->ok, untrusted+traffic->warn device-hint, connection->proxy green, un-probeable->can't-check), a failed action shows warn in its status line not a false done, the Verify prove-it renders the concrete curl as copyable text, P3 puts manual steps behind 'Set it up manually' on an auto OS (inline on non-auto)."
  integration:
    count: 3
    covers: "Core contract (tests/e2e_capture.rs +1): against a real ephemeral core, an untrusted-CA client fails its intercepted TLS handshake and records NO flow, yet bumps GET /stats connections AND emits a 'connection' SSE event carrying the target authority; trusted-https + plain-http paths still yield the expected flows. tests/api.rs (+1): GET /stats reports the note_connection tally. App seam (App.test.tsx +1): a 'connection' event turns the proxy step green ('Receiving traffic', tone ok) while trust shows the not-decrypting device hint, and neither a probe nor a bare connection reveals the list — reveal stays decrypted-flow-only."
  e2e:
    count: 4
    covers: "ui/e2e/specs/onboarding.spec.ts: the UC-5 spine stays green with the new render — fresh launch shows onboarding, a real proxied+decrypted HTTPS request flips Verify green and reveals the list, then the list filters and appends live."
  waived: "The two local OS probes (ca_trusted via 'security'/'certutil'; proxy_status reused from W5 via 'networksetup'/registry) read the real machine and are not hermetically runnable — same class as W2/W3's auto-set commands, epic waiver inherited. Their output is a thin trusted/untrusted/unknown shell-out; the STATUS DERIVATION they feed is fully unit-tested, and the connection signal they complement IS hermetic (a real CONNECT at an ephemeral core) and proven at integration, no waiver. The connection-goes-green-before-decrypt path is asserted at integration, not re-driven in the WebDriver e2e (the harness only drives a trusted proxied request)."
